# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Nothing here is committed.

# The reader, the co-pilot and the analyst are all real model calls. Without a
# key the app still runs: the calculator, the grid, provenance, exports and
# every award scenario work, and the three AI loops refuse honestly rather than
# answering from a lookup table.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Leave LLM_PROVIDER unset for Claude Opus 5, which is what the demo
# should run on: it gives native PDF citations, and that is where the PDF
# supplier's provenance comes from. Set to "gemini" with a GEMINI_API_KEY to run
# the loops on Gemini instead, where the PDF locator falls back to a
# model-reported one and the UI says so.
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Unset locally: the app runs embedded Postgres (PGlite) persisted to .pglite/,
# so it is fully runnable before anyone creates a cloud database. Set to a Neon
# connection string in production and nothing else changes.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Demo protection (lib/demo-guard.ts). Set these on any public deployment.
# With DEMO_ACCESS_CODE set, every route that calls a model (analyst, co-pilot,
# extract, inbox) needs the code once per browser, swapped at /api/access for a
# signed seven-day cookie. Browsing the grid and the exports stays open.
# Unset locally: no gate, and no limits under `npm run dev`.
# DEMO_ACCESS_CODE=
# Signs the access cookie. Optional: derived from the code when unset, in which
# case changing the code also signs everyone out.
# DEMO_COOKIE_SECRET=
# Model requests allowed per IP per 10 minutes. Default 20.
# DEMO_RATE_LIMIT=20
# Model requests allowed per UTC day across everyone. Default 300. Counted in
# requests, not dollars: nothing prices a call at runtime. The rate and the cap
# also apply to a production build with no access code, so a forgotten code
# still leaves a ceiling on the bill.
# DEMO_DAILY_CALL_CAP=300
